    "created_at": "2020-08-11T13:31:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-11T13:33:13Z",
    "body": "I explored to modify the spec but got a blocker. [6.4 Activation behavior of elements](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation) says:\r\n>Certain elements in HTML have an activation behavior, which means that the user can activate them. This is always caused by a click event. \r\n\r\n... but both Firefox and Chrome trigger it without a click event. ~~It seems that fixing this requires modifying [DOM event dispatch algorithm](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dispatching-events), which would become a broader (and dirtier with exceptions) spec change than I thought. What do you think, would it be worth to do that or do you have an alternative way to fix this?~~\r\n\r\nAh never mind, DOM does not care about `disabled`, no need to fix it.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/671948639/reactions",
